The files under NaturalLatents/Upstream/ are adapted from that project at
revision 7b41957da9500716102cba323b3a48af0f23751c, the head of its pull
request #6 by Jeremy Gillen (jezgillen). The first lines of each such file
name its source path and that revision, summarize the changes, and say
whether it comes from upstream's main branch, from pull request #5 as
carried by pull request #6, or from pull request #6 itself; a Local changes
line lists any helper lemmas the file adds, moves or re-proves, among them
reduce_to_connected, re-proved from two one-sided component inequalities.
That revision includes upstream's finite-information
foundation, duality, optimum existence, seed and race machinery, and pull
request #6's coordinate-race, powered-race-winner, contact-information and
probability-table modules. The assembly in this repository follows pull
request #6's method: powered-reference race coding with a coordinate ledger.

NaturalLatents/Statement.lean takes its table definitions (Probability, H,
Hcond, CMI, StochasticError, DeterministicError, deterministicTable) from pull
request #6's stoch_to_det/ReadableStatement.lean at that revision, unchanged
apart from documentation and variable names, and states TableClaim in the form
of its theorem natural_latents_linear_bound with a constant c < 7 in place of
47/5; T, tau and ScoreClaim are added here. The Bridge section of
NaturalLatents/Main.lean (finite_bound, table_bound, table_bound_entropy) is
adapted from pull request #6's stoch_to_det/FiniteBoundProof.lean and
stoch_to_det/TableBoundProof.lean at that revision.

That revision also includes the shared exponential race of pull request #5 by
Satya Benson (satchlj), which pull request #6 carries: the SharedRace/
modules, the clock-race lemmas in Race.lean, the contact secants in
Floor.lean, and first versions of DomFloorCore.lean and PhiBounds.lean, which
pull request #6 revises.

Apart from the adapted material named above (the files under
NaturalLatents/Upstream/, the table definitions in
NaturalLatents/Statement.lean and the Bridge section of
NaturalLatents/Main.lean) and the standard Apache License text, the repository
is the author's own work, building on the upstream definitions and the method
credited above. The files under NaturalLatents/General/ build on the upstream
definitions, which NaturalLatents/General/Definitions.lean imports, and most
of them use those definitions under their upstream names in the namespace
stoch_to_det. They were written in October 2026, after pull request #6. Each
states in its first lines whether it was first written on an unpublished
branch of the author's earlier repository,
https://github.com/AlexisOlson/stochastic-to-deterministic-latents (Lean
package StochasticToDeterministicLatents), and reorganised for this
repository (namespace NaturalLatents.General, declarations renamed, unused
material removed), or written for this repository.
